---
import { SITE, url } from '../../lib/site';
---

<section class="tool" aria-labelledby="ext-title">
  <div class="tool-head">
    <h2 id="ext-title">Before You Give</h2>
    <span class="note">Chrome, Edge and Firefox · collects nothing</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tool-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>What it does</h3>
      <ul class="ext-list">
        <li>On fundraiser pages from GoFundMe, JustGiving and Every.org, it shows a small card with three questions and a “Look it up” button.</li>
        <li>Anywhere, clicking its icon opens the full ten-question <a href={url('/method/#checklist')}>Giver’s Checklist</a> and a lookup pre-filled with the page title.</li>
        <li>It has no analytics or background data transmission. Search text stays in the browser until you choose an external registry.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row ext-actions">
        <a class="btn" href={url('/downloads/charitology-extension.zip')} download>Download the extension (.zip)</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${SITE.repo}/tree/main/extension`}>Read the source</a>
      </div>
      <p class="note"><a href={url('/tools/browser-extension/privacy/')}>Privacy notice</a> · <a href={url('/downloads/charitology-chrome.zip')} download>Chrome store package</a> · <a href={url('/downloads/charitology-firefox.zip')} download>Firefox store package</a></p>
      <h3>Install it</h3>
      <ol class="ext-list">
        <li>Unzip the download.</li>
        <li><strong>Chrome or Edge:</strong> open <code>chrome://extensions</code>, turn on Developer mode, choose <em>Load unpacked</em> and select the unzipped folder.</li>
        <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> open <code>about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox</code>, choose <em>Load Temporary Add-on</em> and pick <code>manifest.json</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="note">Store packages and listing materials are prepared. Submission and store approval are still pending; use a developer install for now. Firefox requires version 140 or later.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>What you’ll see</h3>
      <div class="mock" role="img" aria-label="Preview of the card the extension shows on donation pages">
        <div class="mock-head"><span class="mock-dot"></span> Before you give <span class="mock-x">×</span></div>
        <ol>
          <li>Symptom or source? Where on the chain does this gift act?</li>
          <li>What happens if I don’t give? Would it be funded anyway?</li>
          <li>How would anyone find out if it stopped working?</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="mock-actions"><span class="mock-btn">Look it up</span><span class="mock-btn ghost">All 10 questions</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ext-list {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .ext-actions {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .mock {
    max-width: 340px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--bg);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem 0.9rem;
  }
  .mock-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .mock-dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-wash);
  }
  .mock-x {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
  .mock ol {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .mock li + li {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
  }
  .mock-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .mock-btn {
    padding: 0.4rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--bg);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .mock-btn.ghost {
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
